<title>NEW ZEALAND: Otter Tanami gold mine reopens.</title>
<headline>Otter Tanami gold mine reopens.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Otter Gold Mines said on Tuesday that normal operations at the Tanami Gold Mine, 60 percent owned by Otter and 40 percent by Acacia Resources, were expected to resume next week, following the re-opening of the Alice Springs-Tanami Road to full traffic.</p>
<p>The mine had been operating on a reduced basis to conserve fuel stocks since late February as a consequence of wet weather preventing fuel supplies from reaching the mine site, Otter said. --Wellington Newsroom (64 4) 4734746</p>
</text>
